  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women&apos;s Empowerment Principles Gender Action Labs (Southeast Asia) 2023-30</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UN Women&#x2019;s Asia-Pacific Gender Action Lab (GAL): Innovation and Impact for Gender Equality powered by the Women&#x2019;s Empowerment Principles (WEPs) is a four-year proposal developed by UN Women to further advance private sector and government action to accelerate gender-responsive business policies and practices. It has a regional focus on ASEAN and in four priority countries &#x2013; Indonesia, Philippines, Cambodia and Malaysia. The GAL program seeks to address the &#x2018;action gap&#x2019; between private sector awareness and commitment to gender equality and practical actions taken. It also seeks to support government and regulatory actors with a role in enabling private sector action. The GAL proposes a systematic capacity-building approach paired with practical approaches (Action Labs) to enable accelerated implementation, and a mechanism for policy makers to learn from these solutions to design feasible practice-informed policies to accelerate gender-responsive business conduct in selected focus areas.</narrative>
  </description>
